course: dictionary
lesson: 15651
title: Thereby: linking an action to its result
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words join two ideas together, and «thereby» is one of them. It is a formal word, so you will meet it in exams, science reports and official writing. It means as a result of that, or by doing that.
explain: Look at this sentence: «She saved 5 dollars a week, thereby saving 20 in four weeks.» Saving 5 dollars each week is the action. Saving 20 in four weeks is the result. Thereby points from the action to the result.
explain: A simple check: put «as a result» in place of thereby. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Thereby often comes before an -ing word, as in «thereby helping» or «thereby saving».
fact: Thereby means as a result of that, or by doing that.
fact: «Thereby» is a formal word, so you will see it more in writing and reports than in everyday chat.
fact: «Thereby» links an action to its result, as in «The bridge was closed, thereby stopping the buses.»
fact: Thereby is often followed by an -ing word, such as «thereby helping» or «thereby saving».
exercise: «The farmer planted more trees, thereby giving the birds new homes.» What does thereby mean here? | Next to the birds | Without any trees | Before the trees were planted | *As a result, the birds got new homes
exercise: «He practised the piano every day, thereby improving quickly.» Which phrase has the same meaning as thereby here? | Instead of that | Even though that | Before that | *As a result of that
exercise: «The shop lowered its prices, thereby bringing in more customers.» What is the result? | The shop lowered its prices | The prices went up | *More customers came in | The shop closed for the day
test: «The heavy rain flooded the road, thereby closing the school.» What is the result of the flooding? | The rain stopped | The road was flooded | *The school closed | The children went swimming
test: «Sam finished his homework early, thereby having time to play football.» What does thereby show? | That Sam was never allowed to play | *That finishing early led to time to play | That the homework was hard | That Sam played before doing his homework
exam: «The company cut its costs, thereby making a larger profit for its owners.» Which word joins the action to its result? | company | cut | *thereby | owners
